tion":51,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2518122328","pull_request_review_id":3453195982,"id":2518122328,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6WF39Y","diff_hunk":"@@ -154,29 +161,45 @@ class CommandQueueMT {\n \t}\n \n \tvoid _flush() {\n+\t\tMutexLock lock(mutex);\n+\n \t\tif (unlikely(flush_read_ptr)) {\n \t\t\t// Re-entrant call.\n \t\t\treturn;\n \t\t}\n \n-\t\tMutexLock lock(mutex);\n+\t\tchar *cmd_backup = (char *)alloca(MAX_COMMAND_SIZE);\n \n \t\twhile (flush_read_ptr < command_mem.size()) {\n \t\t\tuint64_t size = *(uint64_t *)&command_mem[flush_read_ptr];\n \t\t\tflush_read_ptr += 8;\n \t\t\tCommandBase *cmd = reinterpret_cast<CommandBase *>(&command_mem[flush_read_ptr]);\n-\t\t\tuint32_t allowance_id = WorkerThreadPool::thread_enter_unlock_allowance_zone(lock);\n-\t\t\tcmd->call();\n-\t\t\tWorkerThreadPool::thread_exit_unlock_allowance_zone(allowance_id);\n+\n+\t\t\t// Protect against against race condition between this thread\n+\t\t\t// during the call to the command and other threads potentially\n+\t\t\t// invalidating the pointer due to reallocs.\n+\t\t\tmemcpy(cmd_backup, (char *)cmd, size);\n+\n+\t\t\tif (unique_flusher) {\n+\t\t\t\t// A single thread will pump; the lock is only needed for the command queue itself.","path":"core/templates/command_queue_mt.h","commit_id":"4ba4558cf6e0550190ee2cb7fbc3c6af3fa2e677","original_commit_id":"bd615b42d4d986526cc8d5cd462ed6ffb60b4473","user":{"login":"RandomShaper","id":11797174,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk3MTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11797174?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper","html_url":"https://github.com/RandomShaper","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Such `if` would indeed prevent concurrent flushing of the queue. However, that wouldn't be enough for memory synchronization. In the case of multiple flusher threads, the lock in this function protects both the command queue data and the \"subject\" data. For instance, any of both physics servers can be flushed both from its dedicated pumping thread and the main thread. If commands targeting that server were left run without the lock held, the two threads would be out-of-sync memory wise.\r\n\r\nThat said, out of the scope of this PR there are two potential enhancements:\r\n- 1) Modify the cases of non-unique-flusher so they always flush from the same thread. That would clear the path towards what you're suggesting.\r\n- 2) On top of the previous point, it'd be worth analyzing if there's any remaining case of \"unlock allowance.\" If not, such feature could be completely removed.","created_at":"2025-11-12T12:29:32Z","updated_at":"2025-11-12T12:29:32Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112506#discussion_r2518122328","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112506","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2518122328"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112506#discussion_r2518122328"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112506"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2518122328/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":181,"original_line":184,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2516111527,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":63,"position":47,"subject_type":"line"}]